(Returning a parameter's list hands back a copy, so changing the result
 leaves the caller's list as it was.)
To 'pass back' with a list called items.
    Return a list, items.

a list called xs is ["a"].
a list called ys is 'pass back' of xs.
Set element 1 of ys to "Z".
append "b" to ys.
Print "xs: {xs}".
Print "ys: {ys}".
